<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What is an indexing conveyor?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>An indexing conveyor advances product a fixed distance and holds it stationary for a downstream operation. Each start-stop cycle positions product at a precise dwell point for filling, labeling, pick-and-place, inspection, or assembly. Accuracy depends on the technology: Dorner rates its 2200 Precision Move servo belt package at ±0.04 in index accuracy, while pallet systems with lift-and-locate stations reach ±0.004 in repeatability (Dorner FlexMove).</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">Servo indexing vs. mechanical indexing?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Servo indexing uses programmable servo motors, change index length, speed, dwell, and motion profile through the HMI. Mechanical indexing uses cams or Geneva drives with fixed motion profiles. Servo costs more but enables recipe-based changeover for multi-SKU lines. Mechanical provides reliable, maintenance-simple operation for dedicated single-format applications.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">What accuracy can indexing conveyors achieve?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>A servo cogged belt indexer locates the belt, not the part: Dorner rates its 2200 Precision Move servo package at ±0.04 in index accuracy. Pallet systems locate a fixtured carrier: Dorner rates its FlexMove lift-and-locate at ±0.004 in repeatability, and Bosch Rexroth states its TS 2plus with TS 2Booster reaches a stop position with an accuracy of up to 0.015 mm. Mechanical cam indexers are rated in arc seconds at the output shaft. Match the technology to the tolerance your downstream operation actually needs.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">What industries use indexing conveyors?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Food and beverage (filling, capping, labeling), pharmaceutical (blister packing, vial filling), cosmetics (tube filling, compact assembly), automotive (parts assembly), and electronics (PCB handling). Any operation requiring precise product positioning for a timed process uses indexing conveyors.</p>

</div>
